pment S-1:\"\ncurl -s -X POST \"$BASE_URL/shipments/S-1/deliver\" | jq .status\n\n# 12. Get order and check fulfilment (should be PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED still, since S-2 is CREATED)\necho -e \"\\n12. Getting order (expect PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED fulfilment):\"\ncurl -s -X GET \"$BASE_URL/orders/O-1\" | jq .fulfilment\n\n# 13. Confirm and deliver S-2\necho -e \"\\n13. Confirming shipment S-2:\"\ncurl -s -X POST \"$BASE_URL/shipments/S-2/confirm\" | jq .status\n\necho -e \"\\n14. Delivering shipment S-2:\"\ncurl -s -X POST \"$BASE_URL/shipments/S-2/deliver\" | jq .status\n\n# 15. Get order and check fulfilment (should be DELIVERED)\necho -e \"\\n15. Getting order (expect DELIVERED fulfilment):\"\ncurl -s -X GET \"$BASE_URL/orders/O-1\" | jq .fulfilment\n\n# 16. Test pagination\necho -e \"\\n16. Testing pagination with limit and offset:\"\ncurl -s -X GET \"$BASE_URL/orders?limit=1&offset=0\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" | jq '.[] | .orderId'\necho \"X-Total-Count header:\"\ncurl -s -X GET \"$BASE_URL/orders?limit=1&offset=0\" -I | grep \"X-Total-Count\"\n\n# 17. Test fulfilment filter\necho -e \"\\n17. Creating another order and testing fulfilment filter:\"\ncurl -s -X POST \"$BASE_URL/orders\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"orderId\":\"O-2\",\"customerId\":\"C-1\",\"amount\":100,\"currency\":\"EUR\",\"quantity\":1}' | jq .\n\necho -e \"\\nListing orders with fulfilment=DELIVERED:\"\ncurl -s -X GET \"$BASE_URL/orders?fulfilment=DELIVERED\" | jq '.[] | .orderId'\n\n# Clean up\nkill $APP_PID\nEOF\n\nchmod +x /tmp/test_features.sh\ntimeout 30 /tmp/test_features.sh 2>/dev/null || true\n"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":33,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Excellent! All tests pass. Let me create a concise summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI've successfully implemented the three features specified in BE-005:\n\n### 1. **Partial Fulfilment**\n- Added `quantity` field to Order and Shipment (default 1, validated > 0)\n- Added `DELIVERED` status to ShipmentStatus enum\n- Created Fulfilment data class tracking allocated, delivered, and status\n- Implemented shipment transitions: CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→DELIVERED, CREATED→CANCELLED\n- Added allocation checking: POST /shipments rejects with 409 if exceeding order quantity\n- Added fulfilment status filter: GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS\n- Added quantity amendment: PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity (validates no reduction below allocated)\n- Cancelled shipments release their quantity (status != CANCELLED in allocation checks)\n\n### 2. **Customer Validation**\n- Added CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND error code with 422 UnprocessableEntityException\n- POST /orders now rejects non-existent customers with 422 through error envelope\n- GET /customers/{customerId} now returns 404 with error envelope\n- Updated OrderControllerTest to create customers before creating orders\n\n### 3. **Paged Lists**\n- Added limit (1-100, default 100) and offset (0+, default 0) to all list endpoints\n- Added X-Total-Count header with total count (after fulfilment filter for orders)\n- Validation: returns 400 for invalid limit/offset\n- All lists sorted by id (orderId, shipmentId, customerId)\n\n### Key Implementation Details\n- Fulfilment status is calculated on-the-fly from current shipments\n- Shipments contribute to \"allocated\" when not CANCELLED\n- Shipments contribute to \"delivered\" when DELIVERED\n- Status transitions are enforced (409 for invalid transitions)\n- Existing tests updated to reflect new requirements\n\n**All 13 tests pass successfully** ✅","t